{{!-- v3 Gear tab.

      SECOND PART MIGRATED. 155 lines on v2, thirteen includes, and — unlike Combat — almost none
      of its debt is floats: the money row and the item list size themselves with fixed-width
      classes (`width-namebox`, `width-mediumbox`, `width-abilitybox`, `width-valuebox`), which is
      what `css/responsive.css` then patches per language. A `<table>` replaces every one of them
      with columns that size to their content, which is the point of the exercise and the reason
      the ES/DE/IT width patches can eventually go.

      SHELL/ROW SPLIT (add-pc-sheet-v3 D5), AND WHERE THIS FILE CANNOT HONOUR IT
      -------------------------------------------------------------------------
      D5 says a v3 template may hold layout and `{{> …}}` includes, may not hold a row renderer,
      and may not emit a `data-action` its v2 counterpart lacks. The third clause holds exactly:
      every `data-action` below (`itemCreate`, `rollDice`, `itemActive`) and every `data-*` is one
      `parts/gear.hbs` already emits, carried across unchanged.

      The second clause CANNOT hold here, and that is a property of the tree rather than a choice.
      There is no shared partial for a gear row: `parts/gear.hbs` renders its own, inline, and the
      only shared thing it calls out to is `list_icons.hbs`. So a v3 shell either duplicates the
      row or invents `gear_itemrow.hbs` — and that partial could not actually be shared, because v2
      needs `<div class="width-namebox">` and v3 needs `<td>`. The row is therefore duplicated
      here, deliberately, and `list_icons.hbs` is still included per type so the icon set and the
      eye's behaviour stay in one file for both sheets.

      THE DRAG CONTRACT, WHICH IS NOT A CSS SELECTOR AND IS NOT COVERED BY binder-selector-check
      ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      `DropHelper.HandleDragDrop` (drop-helpers.js:350-357) does `clone = original.parentElement`
      and then reads `clone.dataset.itemid` — so the DIRECT PARENT of `.draggable` must be the
      element carrying `data-itemid`, or drag-between-actors silently stops working. On v2 that
      parent is `.dragrow`. A `<tr data-itemid>` does NOT satisfy it, because the handle has to
      live in a `<td>`; so `data-itemid` sits on the handle CELL below. Same guarantee, one
      cosmetic difference recorded out loud: the drag ghost is the handle cell rather than the
      whole row.

      THE ELEVEN-BRANCH LADDER IS TEN HERE. `parts/gear.hbs:124-127` tests
      `wod.types.device` TWICE with identical bodies; the second branch is unreachable. Dropping it
      changes nothing that can render, and takes the include count 13 -> 12.

      reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D3 — MUNDANE ONLY. This tab used to list every `Item`/`Fetish`
      document via `getItems`; Wonders (`system.ismagical === true`) and Fetishes now render on the
      Poderes tab instead (right after Rotes), so this tab calls `getMundaneItems` at the two call
      sites that used to call `getItems`: the `{{#if}}` gate and the list passed into the table. The
      empty-state `{{else}}` branch does not call the helper again — it only renders when the
      `{{#if}}` above already resolved falsy. `getItems` itself is untouched and still registered —
      it is what keeps the v2 sheet, which still calls it, identical. The table markup itself moved
      out to `parts/item_table.hbs`, shared with the new Poderes section — see that file's header.

      D7 — the tab's own create control is GONE, not repointed: see the `v3-tabhead` comment below.

      A SECOND SHEET RENDERS THIS FILE (add-chantry-inventory-effects-and-roster, task 3.3)
      ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      `ChantryActorSheetV2` declares this same template as its `gear` PART. The spec requires it —
      "SHALL reuse `templates/actor/v3/gear.hbs` rather than a Chantry-only copy of it, so that a
      change to how gear reads happens once" — and it explicitly forbids getting the markup by
      inheriting `PCActorSheet`/`PCActorSheetV3`, so the sharing has to happen at the FILE, which is
      what this is.

      One flag decides which sheet is rendering: `vault`, set by `prepareItemLists`
      (`module/scripts/gear-lists.js`) for BOTH sheets — `false` on the PC, `true` on a Chantry. It
      is never `undefined`, on purpose: a template reading a key its preparer never built is the one
      defect `test-part-render.mjs` exists to catch, so the flag is always present and the PC's
      branch is the `{{#unless}}` one, i.e. absent-and-falsy could never silently strip the PC's own
      content.

      What `vault` turns OFF is the three blocks a Chantry has no data for — carried/banked money
      and the gear notes prose box (`system.gear.*`, which `template.json`'s "Chantry" simply does
      not have: writing to it would persist junk under a key nothing reads) and the macro rail
      (`macro_icons.hbs` reads the actor's own macro list). What it turns ON is the three extra
      lists a vault needs and a PC does not, because on the PC they live on other tabs: weapons and
      armour (Combate) and Wonders/Fetishes (Poderes). A Chantry has neither of those tabs, so its
      one Equipo tab is where its whole inventory reads.

      THE ITEM LISTS COME OFF THE CONTEXT NOW, not from `(getMundaneItems actor)` inline. Same
      `ItemHelper` calls, same results, one reason: an inline helper call is invisible to
      `test-part-render.mjs`'s missing-context-key check, and a list read off the context is not.
      See `module/scripts/gear-lists.js`'s own header. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-drop-area="true">

	<div class="v3-tabhead">
		{{!-- v2 named this tab "Gear" twice — once in the nav and once in a banner — and named the
		      thing below it nothing at all. One heading, in the content area. --}}
		<h2 class="v3-tabtitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.tab.gear"}}</h2>

		{{!-- reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D7 — NO CREATE CONTROL HERE ANY MORE. `CreateButtonsGear`
		      (the dialog `data-origin="gear"` opened) stamps `ismagical: true` on all nine kinds it
		      mints, unconditionally, and nothing in this system ever clears that flag — so every
		      item this button produced rendered on the Poderes tab, never on this one. The control
		      moved to `v3/powers.hbs`, beside the magical-item list it actually populates. Mundane
		      items reach this tab only by compendium drop or drag from another actor; there is
		      currently no in-sheet route that creates one, which is why the button is gone rather
		      than repointed. --}}
	</div>

	{{!-- Two grid columns: content, and the macro rail. On v2 the rail is `float: right`, so the
	      sections below flow AROUND it and their width depends on how many dice the splat happens
	      to show. As a grid item it cannot float (D4: `float` computes to `none` on a grid item,
	      which beats `!important` because it is not a cascade contest) and it establishes its own
	      formatting context, so nothing in either column can leak into the other. --}}
	<div class="v3-tabbody">
		<div class="v3-tabmain">

			{{!-- PC-ONLY, both of them: a Chantry/Construct actor has no `system.gear` at all
			      (`template.json`'s "Chantry" carries locked/flavor/rating/tier/pool/traits/notes
			      and nothing else), so the money fields would write to a key nothing reads and the
			      prose box would target `system.gear.notes` on a document with no such field. The
			      Chantry's own notes live on its Rasgos tab, where they always have. --}}
			{{#unless vault}}
			<div class="v3-section">
				{{!-- `proseheadline` is passed. It was the ONE omission among description.hbs's
				      eleven callers, which rendered the notes heading as an empty emphasised div
				      until it was fixed today; it stays passed here.

				      NOTE, and this is a live finding rather than a v3 concern: `wod.labels.notes`
				      is an OBJECT node in lang/en.json and lang/es.json (it has `.backgrounds`,
				      `.merits`, … beneath it), not a string. `game.i18n.localize` returns the raw
				      key when the lookup is not a string, so the heading currently reads
				      "wod.tab.notes". Carried across verbatim rather than guessed at, because
				      picking the replacement key is a content decision. --}}
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/description.hbs" proseheadline="wod.tab.notes" locked=locked headline=true prosename="system.gear.notes" prosevalue=gear proseenriched=enrichedGear}}
			</div>

			<div class="v3-section">
				<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.gear.money"}}</h3>

				{{!-- v2 wrapped these two fields in `.clearareaBox > .pullLeft[style="display:flex"]
				      > .area-box`, inside a `.sheet-area` carrying `style="flex-flow: row nowrap"`
				      — a float, a clearfix and two inline styles to place two inputs side by side.
				      A two-column grid does it with none of them.

				      The label WRAPS the input rather than using `for=`/`id`: Foundry can have two
				      PC sheets open at once, and a duplicated `id` would bind both labels to
				      whichever input the document happens to hold first. Implicit association has
				      no such failure mode. v2 used `.floating-label`, which is pure CSS (wod.css:
				      1001-1029) with no binder behind it, so nothing is lost by replacing it.

				      `autofocus` is dropped: BOTH v2 inputs carry it, which is invalid (one per
				      document) and steals focus to the money field whenever the tab renders.
				      `required` is dropped with it — it existed only to drive the `:valid`
				      selector the floating label needed, and on an empty field it makes the form
				      fail native validation. `name`, `data-name` and `data-dtype` are unchanged,
				      which is everything the submit path reads. --}}
				<div class="v3-fields">
					<label class="v3-field">
						<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize "wod.gear.moneycarried"}}</span>
						{{#if locked}}
							<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.gear.money.carried}}" autocomplete="off" readonly />
						{{else}}
							<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.gear.money.carried" type="text" value="{{actor.system.gear.money.carried}}" data-name="data.system.gear.money.carried" data-dtype="Number" autocomplete="off" />
						{{/if}}
					</label>

					<label class="v3-field">
						<span class="v3-fieldlabel">{{localize "wod.gear.moneybank"}}</span>
						{{#if locked}}
							<input class="sheet-infoValues" type="text" value="{{actor.system.gear.money.bank}}" autocomplete="off" readonly />
						{{else}}
							<input class="sheet-infoValues editable" name="system.gear.money.bank" type="text" value="{{actor.system.gear.money.bank}}" data-name="data.system.gear.money.bank" data-dtype="Number" autocomplete="off" />
						{{/if}}
					</label>
				</div>
			</div>
			{{/unless}}

			<div class="v3-section">
				<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.gear.otheritems"}}</h3>

				{{#if mundaneitems}}
					{{!-- A real table: five columns of homogeneous data with a header row, which is
					      what v2 drew with `div.headlineRow` plus five fixed pixel widths. The
					      table gives a screen reader the column association those divs never had,
					      and gives a long Spanish type name somewhere to go. Extracted to
					      `item_table.hbs` (reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D3) so the Poderes tab's
					      magical-item list can share the exact same row markup. --}}
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/item_table.hbs"
						items=mundaneitems actor=actor locked=locked caption="wod.gear.otheritems"}}
				{{else}}
					{{!-- The empty state (D9). v2 drew the four column headers over nothing, which
					      reads as broken rather than as empty. The tab is never hidden and the
					      create control above never moves: it is the only in-sheet route to
					      making this list non-empty.

					      reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 — keyed off `getMundaneItems`, not `getItems`: an
					      actor holding only Wonders/Fetishes (which now render on Poderes) must see
					      THIS empty state here, not a table with zero rows.

					      TWO TEXTS, because the PC's one is FALSE on a vault. `wod.gear.empty` ends
					      "…créalos y consúltalos en la pestaña de Poderes. Las armas y las armaduras
					      van en la pestaña de Combate", and a Chantry HAS NEITHER TAB: `vault: true`
					      is precisely the flag that brings weapons, armour and magical items onto
					      THIS tab (see the block below). So the empty state was sending a GM to two
					      places that do not exist, on the one sheet where everything already lives
					      here — the same class of defect as an affordance that renders nowhere, one
					      step further along: a door that opens onto nothing. One `{{#if vault}}` and
					      a second string, rather than softening the PC's text into something vague
					      enough to be true for both. --}}
					{{#if vault}}
						<p class="v3-empty">{{localize "wod.chantry.vault.empty"}}</p>
					{{else}}
						<p class="v3-empty">{{localize "wod.gear.empty"}}</p>
					{{/if}}
				{{/if}}
			</div>

			{{!-- VAULT ONLY — the three lists a Chantry/Construct needs and the PC does not, because
			      on the PC each of them already renders on a tab a Chantry has no equivalent of:
			      weapons and armour on Combate (`parts/combat_melee.hbs` and siblings, which compute
			      an attack pool from Atributos a Chantry does not have), Wonders and Fetishes on
			      Poderes (`v3/powers.hbs`, reorganize-mage-sheet-v3 D3). A Chantry has ONE inventory
			      tab, so its whole vault reads here, in the four groups the spec names.

			      Each is gated on having content rather than drawing an empty table: the mundane
			      section above already carries this tab's empty state, and four empty tables would
			      say the same nothing four times. Same `item_table.hbs`, same row markup, same
			      `list_icons.hbs` per row — no second copy of any of it. --}}
			{{#if vault}}
				{{#if weapons}}
					<div class="v3-section">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.chantry.vault.weapons"}}</h3>
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/item_table.hbs"
							items=weapons actor=actor locked=locked caption="wod.chantry.vault.weapons"}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{#if armoritems}}
					<div class="v3-section">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.labels.combat.armor"}}</h3>
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/item_table.hbs"
							items=armoritems actor=actor locked=locked caption="wod.labels.combat.armor"}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}

				{{#if magicalitems}}
					<div class="v3-section">
						<h3 class="v3-sectiontitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.power.magicalitems"}}</h3>
						{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/item_table.hbs"
							items=magicalitems actor=actor locked=locked caption="wod.power.magicalitems"}}
					</div>
				{{/if}}
			{{/if}}

		</div>

		{{!-- PC-only: `macro_icons.hbs` renders the actor's own macro rail, and a Chantry has no
		      macros, no dice pool and nothing to roll. --}}
		{{#unless vault}}
		<aside class="v3-macrorail">
			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/macro_icons.hbs"}}
		</aside>
		{{/unless}}
	</div>

</section>
